From 827c3f4f931758ac343203a6945eaf5e6bb33a77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:48:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: one OWNER_WRITTEN source; origin_link_fields
 means enabled and not recorded stopped; pin the done-row carry

Follow-up to PR #2157 (review 5890952298 at d5a7122d12, card t_01a1d4e0d644b672).

1. OWNER_WRITTEN was defined in both hermes_cli/kanban_origin_creation.py and
   tools/kanban_tools_board_delivery.py. The origin side now imports the owner's
   constant. RED: test_owner_written_wire_value_has_one_source failed on main
   ('OWNER_WRITTEN' assigned in kanban_tools_board_delivery); GREEN after.

2. origin_link_fields said "sync runs" but checks sync_enabled() and not
   runstate.down(). No positive running marker exists (a completed round deletes
   the record), so an enabled sync that has not started yet still answers
   owner_written. That direction is fine: the link row waits in the owner's own
   outbox and goes out with its first round, and a refusal to start or a crash
   records a stop. The docstring (and the board_delivery comment) now say
   "enabled and not recorded stopped"; test_owner_answer_means_enabled_and_not_recorded_stopped
   pins both sides with a real runstate file (no record -> answer; record_down -> {}).

3. Done-row carry, checked against the real hub: the owner's hermes-hub
   advance_origin_create finishes with {**creation, ok, code: origin_bound,
   handoff_complete: True, origin_receipt}, where creation is the courier create's
   own result; the origin's fetch_outcomes stores the result verbatim in sent.result.
   Hub req_ledger row placement:macbook:24a806162e8729d0b6f2bf21 (11-13 11:32, before
   #2157 deployed) keeps every creation key that way (origin_creation, placement,
   gated, ...), and origin_chat_link sits in the same dict as origin_creation, so it
   survives. test_owner_answer_survives_the_hubs_done_row_to_the_origin drives the
   real courier create output through that merge into await_task_id/owner_chat_link
   (replacing reliance on a hand-built row). Pin, green on main.

Tests: 9 affected files, 195 passed (hermes-core-wt test).
